# GROUNDED NO MORE

**A single missing part can ground an aircraft. Know which ones, where, and what to do about it.**

[![CI](https://github.com/akashgajjar07-hue/grounded-no-more/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/akashgajjar07-hue/grounded-no-more/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
![Python 3.11+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.11%2B-22C7B8)
[![Licence: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/licence-MIT-B9C8D6)](LICENSE)

**Web app (GitHub Pages):** <https://akashgajjar07-hue.github.io/grounded-no-more/>

![GROUNDED NO MORE: Mission Control view](docs/assets/readme/hero.png)

An aviation spare-parts intelligence project for a fictional airline, **Falcon Hub Airways (fictional)**. It forecasts sparse, removal-driven demand, sizes rotable floats against repair turnaround, decides what to hold at the hub and what to push to outstations, and shows how much material shortage exposure each extra dirham of spares capital removes. Everything runs from one seeded pipeline and ends in a static web app a materials planner could use on a Monday morning.

> **All airline data in this project is simulated: every screen is a simulated planning snapshot.** Station coordinates are real (OurAirports). Every parameter is in [`config/assumptions.yaml`](config/assumptions.yaml) with a provenance tag. Nothing here is measured aviation reliability or any operator's data.

---

## Headline

Holdout results: {{RESULT:seeds.n}} paired seeds ({{RESULT:seeds.holdout}}), 52 weeks (weeks {{RESULT:seeds.kpi_weeks}}), central world, run once after the freeze. "Material AOG" means expected material-related downtime hours: the hours an aircraft waits for a part that was not available in time, including fitting and release-to-service time. The scope is the modelled catalogue of {{RESULT:scope.pn_count}} AOG-critical part numbers, not every part on the fleet.

{{RESULT:core.headline}}

P2 is not a free repositioning of P0's float. Going from P0 to P2 buys {{RESULT:policy.remix.buy_units}} rotables (about {{RESULT:policy.remix.buy_aed}}) for no-go (D0) items and sheds {{RESULT:policy.remix.shed_units}} high-value deferrable ones (about {{RESULT:policy.remix.shed_aed}}), so procurement would see a purchase request plus disposals, at roughly flat net capital (target units × unit cost from the policy tables).

{{RESULT:fo.headline}}

**Findings that do not flatter the method**, kept visible on purpose:

- **Forecasting champions rarely won on the holdout.** The frozen champion was best in only {{RESULT:honest.champions_best}} demand-class × part-class cells. For intermittent rotables the frozen {{RESULT:honest.ir_champion}} champion ranked {{RESULT:honest.ir_rank}} ({{RESULT:honest.ir_best}} was best in hindsight). The policies size rotables on the reliability-exposure rate instead, so they do not depend on that cell's champion.
- **History beats the vendor quote on reliability.** The history-based MTBUR estimate is about {{RESULT:honest.mtbur_hist}} off the hidden truth against about {{RESULT:honest.mtbur_quote}} for vendor quotes (median absolute log error, {{RESULT:honest.mtbur_n}} removal-driven parts).
- **Immediate fill is slightly lower under the network plans.** Against P0, P2 changes the share of requests filled from the shelf by {{RESULT:policies.P2_vs_P0.delta_fill_pts}} {{RESULT:policies.P2_vs_P0.delta_fill_pts_ci}} and P1 by {{RESULT:policies.P1_vs_P0.delta_fill_pts}} {{RESULT:policies.P1_vs_P0.delta_fill_pts_ci}}. The cause is lean consumable and expendable reorder points, not rotables ({{RESULT:policies.fill_by_class}}).
- **Everything depends on the AOG recovery routes.** Every policy, P0 included, leans on robbery at the hub (used automatically as the first AUH route after local stock, with engineering/quality approval flagged), local borrow at outstations, exchange/loan and local buy: {{RESULT:honest.routes_off}}. See [LIMITATIONS](LIMITATIONS.md#economics-and-decisions).
- **Two model limits a domain reviewer flagged, disclosed rather than fixed.** Robbed donor aircraft are assumed grounded until reinstated, but those hours (about {{RESULT:limits.donor_h_per_yr}} a year in the P0 history) are not counted, so absolute downtime is understated for every policy. And {{RESULT:limits.p0_out_brakes}} of P0's {{RESULT:limits.p0_out_total}} outstation rotables are brakes that are only changed at AUH, so the P2-vs-P0 gap largely measures stocking no-go items at line stations. See [LIMITATIONS](LIMITATIONS.md) items 29–39.
- **Selection carried over to the holdout:** {{RESULT:honest.consistency}}.
- **The stress worlds sit at different ends of the calibration band:** {{RESULT:honest.band_ends}}.

A v1 world was archived after a domain review; see [archive/v1](archive/v1/README.md). Its numbers are not findings.

